# Structure checks and refactoring rhythm

## Two modes (do not mix in one turn unless the user explicitly asks)

1. **Implementation / modernization step** — deliver the scoped change; keep diffs minimal. If you notice structural debt, **do not** start a wide refactor here. Add a short entry to the right backlog file (see below) or extend an existing item.

2. **Refactor / structure pass** — only when the user asks (e.g. «проход рефакторинга», «разобрать бэклог», «привести структуру»). Then work from `docs/backlog/refactor-backend.md` or `docs/backlog/refactor-frontend.md`, one theme per session when possible.

## Backlog (single source of planned refactors)

- **Backend (Python, layout under repo root):** `docs/backlog/refactor-backend.md`
- **Frontend (ui/):** `docs/backlog/refactor-frontend.md`

**Entry format (copy block per item):**

```markdown
### [OPEN] Short title
- **Area:** package or path (e.g. `science_graphrag/api/`)
- **Issue:** what is wrong or risky
- **Proposal:** concrete steps (files/modules)
- **Acceptance:** how we know it is done
- **Raised:** YYYY-MM-DD (optional: PR or branch)
```

Mark done with `[DONE]` and a one-line note; do not delete history without user request.

## After a large modernization step

- Run the usual quality gates (see `pre-commit-checklist.mdc`, `backend-quality.mdc`, `frontend-quality.mdc`).
- Append backlog items for **follow-up structure** (imports, layering, duplication, API surface), not for cosmetic nits already fixed in the same PR.

## What this rule does *not* replace

- Automated CI, linters, and tests — they run on every push; this rule is for **human/agent scheduling** of deeper refactors.
